## Coding standards (PHPCS / PHPCBF)

Each contrib module ships its own `phpcs.xml`. **Always detect and use it** — do not hardcode `--standard=Drupal` alone, as modules like `ai` add `DrupalPractice` too.

Two equivalent invocation styles — both work:

```bash
# From project root, using host PHP (faster, no ddev overhead)
php vendor/bin/phpcs --standard=web/modules/contrib/<module>/phpcs.xml <path>
php vendor/bin/phpcbf --standard=web/modules/contrib/<module>/phpcs.xml <path>

# Inside ddev (e.g. from a script or when host PHP differs)
ddev exec phpcs --standard=/var/www/html/web/modules/contrib/<module>/phpcs.xml /var/www/html/<path>
ddev exec phpcbf --standard=/var/www/html/web/modules/contrib/<module>/phpcs.xml /var/www/html/<path>
```

If a module has no `phpcs.xml`, fall back to `--standard=Drupal --extensions=php,module,inc,install,test,profile,theme,info,engine,yml`.

Walk **up** from the target file toward the project root to find the nearest `phpcs.xml` — submodules (e.g. `ai_agents/modules/ai_agents_views/`) inherit the parent module's config.

